+# Refactoring Task: Multi-Attempt Competitive Programming Solver
+
+## Summary of Requirements
+
+### Current State
+- `coding_agent.py`: Single `forward()` method that makes one agent call
+- Single linear workflow, no feedback mechanism
+- No test harness or comparison of candidates
+
+### Target Architecture
+
+1. **Phase 1: Test Building** (build_tests)
+   - Single agent session creates shared test harness in `tests_work/` directory
+   - Output files:
+     - `brute.py`: Simple, obviously-correct implementation
+     - `gen.py`: Test generator that takes `<seed> <mode>`
+       - Modes: tiny/random/edge/max
+     - `samples/`: Directory with every sample from problem statement
+     - Optional: `checker.py` for multiple valid answers
+   - Brute force must reproduce all sample outputs
+
+2. **Phase 2: K Solve Attempts** (solve_attempt)
+   - K=3 (configurable) independent attempts with fresh message history
+   - Different strategy hints per attempt
+   - Each writes only to `attempts/attempt_i/solution.py`
+   - Must pass samples and stress tests before finishing
+
+3. **Phase 3: Evaluate Candidates** (evaluate_candidates)
+   - New tool: `tools/evaluate_candidates.py`
+   - Takes:
+     - List of candidate solution paths
+     - brute_path, generator_path, optional checker_path
+     - num_seeds, timeout, samples_dir, max_input_path
+   - Returns detailed report:
+     - Per-candidate: sample pass/fail
+     - Per-candidate: random-test pass counts per mode
+     - First failing input saved to file with expected vs. actual output
+     - Max-input runtime measurement
+     - TLE/RE treated as failures
+     - Pairwise disagreement count between candidates
+     - Final ranking score
+   - Checker interface: argv `input expected actual`, exit code 0 = pass
+
+4. **Phase 4: Reflection Rounds** (reflect_round)
+   - If no candidate passes everything: another round (bounded, max 2-3)
+   - Agent receives:
+     - Best candidate's code
+     - Concrete failing inputs with expected/actual outputs and timing
+     - Previous notes
+   - Must write root-cause diagnosis before fixing
+   - Later attempts receive summary of earlier failures
+
+5. **Phase 5: Finalization** (finalize)
+   - Copy best-scoring candidate to required solution location
+   - Remove scratch files not in patch
+   - Re-run samples as final sanity check
+
+### Code Structure Changes
+
+#### In coding_agent.py
+- Split `forward()` into helper methods:
+  1. `build_tests()` - create test harness
+  2. `solve_attempt(i, hint, prior_feedback)` - run single attempt
+  3. `evaluate_candidates()` - compare all candidates
+  4. `reflect_round(attempt_num)` - iterate if needed
+  5. `finalize()` - copy winner and cleanup
+- Use `for attempt in range(K)` and `for round in range(MAX_ROUNDS)` only
+- Each helper calls `chat_with_agent` with fresh msg_history and focused prompt
+- Solver prompts: write to own attempt directory, don't modify shared tests
+
+#### New Tool: evaluate_candidates.py
+- Location: `tools/evaluate_candidates.py`
+- Schema (correctly nested):
+  - properties: solution_paths (array of strings), brute_path, generator_path, checker_path (optional), num_seeds (int), timeout_sec (number), samples_dir, max_input_path (optional)
+  - required: ["solution_paths", "brute_path", "generator_path", "num_seeds", "timeout_sec", "samples_dir"]
+- Calls generator with: `python3 gen.py <seed> <mode>`
+- Checker interface: argv: input_file, expected_file, actual_file; exit code 0 = OK
+- Careful to treat TLE/RE as failures
+- Output: Text report with detailed ranking
+
+#### Improve run_tests.py
+- Seeded and mode-aware generator calls: `python3 gen.py <seed> <mode>`
+- Save failing input to disk
+- Standardized checker interface (argv: input_file, expected_file, actual_file)
+- Per-test timeouts
+
+### Prompts
+- Include constraints vs. complexity statement requirement
+- Reflection prompt: include last failing case and diagnosis first
+- Pass accumulated feedback to later attempts:
+  - Previous code summary
+  - Failing inputs
+  - Results from prior rounds
+
+### Correctness Checklist
+- forward() performs: build_tests → K attempts → evaluate → up to N reflection rounds → finalize
+- All loops are bounded (no `while True`)
+- Tool schemas follow conventions (required/properties at correct nesting level, all properties typed)
+- Evaluation report has: failing input, expected/actual output
+- Final repo state contains best-verified solution
